P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Particular sensitivity to calcium channel blockers of the fast inward voltage-dependent sodium current involved in the invasive properties of a metastastic breast cancer cell line</article-title><source>Br J Pharmacol</source><year>2004</year><volume>141</volume><fpage>610</fpage><lpage>615</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14744811</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.bjp.0705649</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yoshida</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ishibashi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Nishio</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Antiproliferative effect of Ca2+ channel blockers on human epidermoid carcinoma A431 cells</article-title><source>Eur J Pharmacol</source><year>2003</year><volume>472</volume><fpage>23</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12860469</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0014-2999(03)01831-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>YS</given-names></name><name><surname>Sayeed</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wurster</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inhibition of cell growth and intracellular Ca2+ mobilization in human brain tumor cells by Ca2+ channel antagonists</article-title><source>Mol Chem Neuropathol</source><year>1994</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>95</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7522451</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yao</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Kwan</surname><given-names>HY</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Activity of 